{
  "id": "ss.lib.relic-plate",
  "name": "Beetle-helm plate",
  "description": "The ground a ruins find is shown on, built as a piece of beetle rather than as a slot: a chitin shell domed at the top into a lit pronotum with a ridge down it, tapering to a tip where the wing-case seam splits the bottom edge, two spiracles on the flanks, and a dark visor cut through the middle for the find to sit in. The light inside it is gold — the shell is the insect, the glow is the age. Every find composes this via `use`, so the twenty-odd of them share one definition and the plate lifts off in one line: the `glyph` variant each of them declares removes this part and nothing else. The `curse` variant drops the shell to dead carapace and turns the light arcane, the two colours the ruins outcome already switches between.",
  "tags": ["ss-lib"],
  "size": [32, 32],
  "parts": [
    {"id": "edge", "shape": {"kind": "poly", "points": [[0, -17.02], [6.41, -16.17], [11.75, -13.39], [14.52, -8.9], [16.23, -3.14], [16.23, 5.4], [13.45, 12.24], [7.47, 16.29], [0, 17.15], [-7.47, 16.29], [-13.45, 12.24], [-16.23, 5.4], [-16.23, -3.14], [-14.52, -8.9], [-11.75, -13.39], [-6.41, -16.17]]}, "fill": "$ink"},
